---
// pitomd.com/guides/claude — connect an Anthropic API key to Pito Studio
// for the AI features (auto-cut drafts, footage-aware answers in the
// Claude split). Linked verbatim from Studio's own setup wizard as
// "pitomd.com/guides/claude" (internal/ui/studio_cockpit_wizard_render.go,
// wizPhClaudeCreds).
//
// Written for a non-technical reader (owner: "the canonical reader is my
// wife") — "API key" is named once, plainly, and the config.toml aside sits
// at the end of "How it's handled," never the lead.
//
// console.anthropic.com now 301-redirects to platform.claude.com
// (verified live 2026-07) — linked directly at the new address rather than
// through the old one.
//
// SOURCE OF TRUTH: pito-tui's README.md ("Configuration" — the `[claude]`
// table: api_key, model, max_tokens; "Leave the table out or the key blank
// to keep the split off; it opens and says so honestly instead of
// pretending to be live"). Unlike IGDB, there is no dedicated Settings-
// surface form for editing the Claude key later — it's set during the
// wizard's first run, or by hand-editing config.toml afterward.

import GuideLayout from "../../layouts/GuideLayout.astro";

const TITLE = "Connect Claude — Pito Studio guides";
const DESCRIPTION =
  "How to create an Anthropic API key and connect Claude to Pito Studio's AI features — what you need, why it's useful, and how it's kept private.";

const pageUrl = new URL("/guides/claude/", Astro.site).href;
const jsonLd = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@graph": [
    {
      "@type": "HowTo",
      name: TITLE,
      url: pageUrl,
      description: DESCRIPTION,
    },
  ],
};
---

<GuideLayout
  title={TITLE}
  description={DESCRIPTION}
  eyebrow="AI features · Claude"
  heading="Connect Claude."
  dek="Claude is what gives Studio its AI features — rough-cut drafts and answers about your own footage — and it never touches anything without you saying yes first. It takes one key from Anthropic's own site."
  slug="claude"
  jsonLd={jsonLd}
>
  <section id="need">
    <h2>What you need</h2>
    <ul class="guide-checklist">
      <li>
        <strong>An Anthropic account with a payment method added</strong> — this kind
        of access is billed by actual use, directly by Anthropic.
      </li>
      <li><strong>About five minutes.</strong></li>
      <li>
        <strong>The right kind of account:</strong> a Claude.ai chat subscription
        (Pro or Max) is a different product and won't work here. You need a developer
        key instead, with its own credits behind it.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section id="why">
    <h2>Why Studio wants this</h2>
    <p>
      Claude is what powers Studio's AI features: rough-cut drafts of a
      timeline, and answers about your own footage inside the Claude panel —
      press <span class="guide-key">c</span> to open it. Studio never acts on your
      footage without you saying yes first: Claude suggests, you decide.
    </p>
    <p>
      Skip this and the rest of Studio works exactly the same; the Claude panel
      just opens and says plainly that it isn't set up yet, instead of
      pretending to be ready.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="handled">
    <h2>How it's handled</h2>
    <div class="guide-callout">
      <p>
        The key you paste in stays right here on this computer, and every
        request goes straight from your machine to Anthropic — nothing passes
        through a Pito server in between.
      </p>
      <p>
        You're billed directly by Anthropic, at their normal rates — Studio
        doesn't add anything on top or track it separately. You can turn the key
        off any time from Anthropic's own site, and the Claude panel goes back
        to its plain "not set up" message.
      </p>
      <p>
        Technically minded: the key lives in the <code>[claude]</code> table of Studio's
        <code>config.toml</code>, alongside which model to use and how long an
        answer is allowed to run.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="steps">
    <h2>Step by step</h2>
    <ol class="guide-steps">
      <li>
        <h3>Sign in to Anthropic's developer site</h3>
        <p>
          Open <a href="https://platform.claude.com/">platform.claude.com</a> — Anthropic's
          developer console, recently renamed from console.anthropic.com to Claude
          Platform — and sign in, or create an account.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3>Add a payment method</h3>
        <p>
          This kind of access is billed by use, separately from any Claude.ai
          chat subscription — add a card under Billing if you haven't already.
          Studio's AI features are billed the normal way, like any other use of
          the service.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3>Create a key</h3>
        <p>
          Go to the API Keys page, click Create Key, and give it a name — <code
            >Pito Studio</code
          > works fine. Anthropic shows you the key exactly once, so copy it before
          you leave the page.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3>Paste it into Studio</h3>
        <p>
          In Studio's setup wizard, say yes when it asks about turning AI on,
          then paste the key in and press <span class="guide-key">Enter</span> to
          save.
        </p>
      </li>
    </ol>
  </section>

  <section id="limits">
    <h2>Good to know</h2>
    <div class="guide-callout guide-callout--limits">
      <p>
        <strong>A chat subscription is not the same thing.</strong> This is the most
        common mix-up: paying for Claude.ai chat (Pro or Max) doesn't give you this
        kind of key. You need a separate one, billed separately, even if you already
        pay for the chat app.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>You're billed for what you use.</strong> There's no flat monthly price
        here — you pay Anthropic for exactly what Studio's AI features use.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>A couple of extra settings live alongside the key.</strong> Studio's
        settings file also lets you choose which model to use and put a ceiling on
        how long an answer can run, if you'd like a bit more control over cost.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Studio is honest if it's missing.</strong> Leave the key out, or take
        it out later, and the Claude panel simply says it isn't set up — never a crash,
        never a silent failure somewhere else in the app.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="done">
    <h2>Back in Studio</h2>
    <div class="guide-callout guide-callout--done">
      <span class="guide-callout__tag">Last step</span>
      <p>
        Going through the setup wizard for the first time? Pasting the key there
        is all it takes — it's ready as soon as Studio opens. Adding or changing
        it later doesn't have its own screen yet: open Studio's settings file,
        add the key under <code>[claude]</code>, and restart Studio. Either way,
        press <span class="guide-key">c</span> anywhere to open the Claude panel once
        it's set.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</GuideLayout>
